{"id":"int-be03f20f87646f3db6f597448de8995c","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-26T10:10:51.773298Z","actor":"T","issue_id":"AI-CLI-cfb","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Fixed + merged dd6e61d (2026-07-26). VERDICT: test drift, not a code regression — 'cdp start' still uses 'open -na' (tunnel.py:272) and finds/writes the PID (tunnel.py:296) exactly as asserted. The macOS tests hardcoded port 9222 / cdp-9222.pid, but cdp start auto-increments off a busy port, and a live CDP Chrome on 9222 is the normal state on this Mac — so the code correctly moved to 9223 and the assertions failed. The Linux tests already pinned _port_in_use false; the macOS ones were added later without the equivalent fixture.\n\nFix adds that fixture, preserving every behavioral assertion rather than relaxing any. NO test was skipped, xfailed or deleted to make the gate green.\n\nVerified by the driver, not accepted from the agent: test_cdp.py 63 passed; full suite in the main tree 1858 passed, 0 failed. Two agents independently reached the same root cause. Unblocks AI-CLI-125."}}
